  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/icon/ICON_0002104">
    <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A person knows an issue, a place, a taxon or a habitat type through their work: the projects, programs and plans they lead and the papers and reports they wrote address it, or the source records say so. Expertise is never passed down from the organizations a person belongs to.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The explorer entails it from the issues, counties, ecoregions, taxa and habitat types a person's led or authored record states itself. A statewide record gives no place expertise, and a record that names more than 10 of one kind gives none of that kind (#1130). Expertise in a component issue is expertise in its integrated issues too, and expertise in a vegetation or CMECS type is expertise in its broader types (#1409, #1410).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/icon/people.owl"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has expertise in</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:nodeID="cbd2eabbd1696134705a184c89b119fefd50c38045ca829b73bb9fcaefd720ed5a"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/icon/ICON_0002105"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="cb1a13edb7247a2bf6a0114614e24852f159ff6fd1bf64bc3d578dd565b00ea6d95"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="cb27e89810f5649b67c5f2c03d21f222fc09bb71aba619cec5d242a7bc6d10d7917"/>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/knowsAbout"/>
